  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1231 PM CDT Tue Sep 8 2026\n\nThe high pressure ridge weakens to some degree by Wednesday and \nThursday. This weakening of the ridge will coincide with an \nincrease in moisture across the region. Models continue to show an\nincrease in rain shower and thunderstorm activity on both of \nthese days as a result. Thursday seems to be the most likely \ntimeframe to see rain as there is a medium chance (30-40%) in \nplace. Some brief gusty winds (up to 40 MPH) and lightning are \nthe main hazard with this activity.\n\nThen, for the remainder of the week and next weekend, the heat\nmakes a return to the region under a slightly stronger high\npressure. Highs will approach 104 degrees again across the Big\nCountry. Overall, the hot and dry conditions will make a return by\nthe end of the forecast period.",
